review:
This game plays well, and has a decent amount of content given the price point and the expectation it sets;

But it has some weird systems incorporated into it, like some of the crafting recipes being locked behind a shop in the main menu. You can earn the currency needed to buy them so it isn't pay-to-win. But it isn't not pay to win. To get to the highest tier tools you need about 21 of this currency for each tool. You get 2 of the currency for each boss you beat. That means you need 41 boss kills just to get the tools. Very off-putting given the game isn't that huge and survival games aren't exactly the most replayable.

Pick it up on sale if you want a day or two's entertainment. Otherwise, just get Valheim.
